      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "basic_script.py :\n\n__name__ is a special built-in-variable in python\nPython automatically sets its value when a file is run or imported.\n\nentry point of a program\n\nWhy is this useful?\n\nPrevents code from running automatically when importing\n\nMakes code reusable (modules, libraries)\n\nVery important for projects, ML apps, Streamlit apps, CLI tools\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "basic_script.py :\n\n__name__ is a special built-in-variable in python\nPython automatically sets its value when a file is run or imported.\n\nentry point of a program\n\nWhy is this useful?\n\nPrevents code from running automatically when importing\n\nMakes code reusable (modules, libraries)\n\nVery important for projects, ML apps, Streamlit apps, CLI tools\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
